> \[!IMPORTANT\]
> This software is **Graduated** and subject to ECMWF's guidelines on [Software Maturity](https://github.com/ecmwf/codex/raw/refs/heads/main/Project%20Maturity).

**earthkit-meteo** is a Python package providing meteorological computations using array (NumPy, Torch and CuPy), xarray or fieldlist. It is part of the [earthkit](https://github.com/ecmwf/earthkit) ecosystem.

## Quick Start

```python

    from earthkit.meteo import thermo

    # using Numpy arrays
    import numpy as np

    t = np.array([264.12, 261.45])  # Kelvins
    p = np.array([850, 850]) * 100.0  # Pascals
    theta = thermo.potential_temperature(t, p)

    # using Torch tensors
    import torch

    t = torch.tensor([264.12, 261.45])  # Kelvins
    p = torch.tensor([850.0, 850.0]) * 100.0  # Pascals
    theta = thermo.potential_temperature(t, p)
```

## Installation

Install via `pip` with:

```
$ pip install earthkit-meteo
```

Alternatively, install via `conda` with:

```
$ conda install earthkit-meteo -c conda-forge
```

